  "answer": "Read twice (Q1, Q2), all 6 scored cases agree; the page verified clean after. CAP-Y2BAR's Heading 1, typed in 4 steps, sits at frame 523 with the text bar and caret. With the frame at its top, Cmd+A and Backspace empty it (1/2/3/10) and Cmd+Z brings it back (1/2/31/10), bar and caret kept throughout; the frame back at 523 keeps them too. Cmd+Shift+Z, emptying it again, pulls the frame's scroll from 523 to 360 and takes the bar and the caret, the edit focused: as the Cmd+Z of CAP-Y2BAR.json. Scored against CAP-Y2REDOPULL2-PREDICTED.json (ours before #565): 5 of 5; rival U (only Cmd+Z takes them) misses the redo. Named misses, not built: the emptied Heading 1 takes 2 rows on the oracle, ours 3 (section 9), so ours' page stays long enough that a redo at 523 doesn't pull there; ours pulls from its own frame's end. S1 and S2, unscored, built twice alike: with the frame at its end (1506, the block wholly above the view) the block is unselected (data-is-selected false), the bar and the frame's selection are gone, the frame's ProseMirror keeps the focus; keys x and y then type at the text's start (193 to 195, caret at 2) and the frame scrolls to 235 to show them; the frame back at its top shows no bar. Overlap with U9 (#565, chrome's): the oracle lets the selection go but keeps the editor live, where ours finishes the edit; named there, not built here."
